\section*{Appendix F: ISSEOM GUI-PDS Visualization Engine Specification}

\subsection*{F.1 Multi-Pane Dashboard Architecture}
The ISSEOM GUI-PDS visualization engine renders simulation sectors in a modular
dashboard grid. Each pane corresponds to a physics domain and displays real-time
tensor fields, stability indicators, and cryptographic verification stamps.

The dashboard layout is defined as:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{G} =
\left\{
G_{i,j} \mid i = 1,\dots,M;\; j = 1,\dots,N
\right\},
\end{equation}
where $G_{i,j}$ is a visualization pane and $(M,N)$ is typically $(4,4)$ or $(3,4)$.

\subsection*{F.2 Sector Rendering Pipeline}
Each sector $D_k$ is rendered using a domain-specific visualization operator
$\mathcal{V}_k$:
\begin{equation}
G_{i,j} = \mathcal{V}_k(\mathbf{X}_{i,j}, \mathcal{F}(t)),
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{X}_{i,j}$ is the local tensor state and $\mathcal{F}(t)$ the fused
telemetry tensor.

Examples include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item MHD flux vector overlays for Sector D-0100
    \item Lattice strain wireframes for Sector D-0200
    \item Gravitational lensing distortion maps for Sector D-0300
    \item Covariance matrix fidelity indicators for Sector D-0700
    \item Multi-frequency spectrograms for Sector D-0850
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{F.3 Real-Time Stability Indicators}
Each pane displays a stability indicator computed from the residual error:
\begin{equation}
\sigma_k(t) =
\exp\left(
-\frac{\epsilon_k(t)}{\tau_k}
\right),
\end{equation}
where $\epsilon_k(t)$ is the sector-specific residual and $\tau_k$ the stability threshold.

Indicators include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Green: $\sigma_k(t) > 0.9$
    \item Yellow: $0.7 < \sigma_k(t) \le 0.9$
    \item Red: $\sigma_k(t) \le 0.7$
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{F.4 Cryptographic Verification Overlays}
Each pane includes a cryptographic verification block containing:
\begin{equation}
\left( C_t,\; \pi_t,\; H_t \right),
\end{equation}
where $C_t$ is the ML-KEM commitment, $\pi_t$ the zk-SNARK proof, and $H_t$ the
homomorphic encryption hash.

These overlays ensure tamper-evident visualization of all rendered states.

